@startuml
' Main flow: Player initiates play request
P -> UI: Select hand card, initiate [Play Card] request
UI -> GE: Submit play request (PlayerID, CardID, Target)
GE -> GRV: Delegate play legality validation
GRV --> GE: Return validation result (Pass/Fail + Reason)

' Alternative branch: Validation result (matches course alt standard)
alt Play rule validation passed
    GE -> CM: Execute card play processing
    CM -> PM: Remove the card from player's hand
    CM --> GE: Return card processing result (CardType, PlayZone)
    GE -> PM: Update player turn state (Remaining actions -1)
    PM --> GE: Return updated player state

    ' Optional branch: Card has active effect (matches course opt standard)
    opt Card contains active effect
        GE -> GE: Execute card effect logic (Draw/Collect rent/Swap property etc.)
        GE -> CM: Update card/deck state (e.g., draw, discard)
        GE -> PM: Update player asset/hand state
    end

    GE -> UM: Sync global game state, trigger UI refresh
    UM --> UI: Update player hand, field cards, action count display
    UI --> P: Display [Play Successful] prompt
else Play rule validation failed
    UI --> P: Display [Play Failed] + Failure reason (e.g., Insufficient actions, Invalid target)
end

@enduml